# The scenes of the architecture-rules deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# architecture-rules.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in architecture-rules.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add ArchUnit to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/archunit/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependency
note "Step 2: add it as a test dependency of the lesson. There is nothing to configure."
show lessons/architecture-rules/example/build.gradle.kts "/libs.archunit/" "lesson build file" --zoom 9

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: the admin page of a shop, as it is today. It reads *storage* directly."
show TodaysSummaryPage 6 19 "web layer: the admin page today" --zoom 17

## Scene 4: the unit tests
note "Ordinary *unit tests*: they check the page gives the right answer."
show OrderSummaryPageTest 14 30 "unit tests" --zoom 27-28

## Scene 5: the architecture rule
note "The *architecture rule*: which layer may use which."
show LayerRulesTest 18 33 "architecture rule" --zoom 20-21 --mark 31

## Scene 6: the rule finds the shortcut
note "Run the tests against the admin page as it is today:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:architecture-rules:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The unit tests pass. The rule names every place the web layer reaches into storage."

## Scene 7: the page that goes through the service
note "The admin page that asks the service layer instead:"
show SummaryPage 6 19 "web layer: the admin page, fixed" --zoom 17
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:architecture-rules:test"
callout "Every layer uses only the layer below it, and the rule keeps it that way."
